\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces (a)~A binary tree with data at its leaves is a shape --- the tree with the data erased, with internal nodes~$\bullet $ and leaf positions~$\circ $ --- together with an assignment of data to the positions, as in \cite  {AbbottAltenkirchGhaniMcBride04}. Positions occur wherever there is a leaf, at any depth. (b)~Flattening as an adapter from the tree interface to the list interface. The shape map sends the skeleton $s$ to its number of leaves, $\ensuremath  {\mathit  {Sum}}\,s = 3$; the position map $\ensuremath  {\mathit  {flat}}_s$ sends batch slot $i$ to the $i$-th leaf from the left, whatever its depth. It is a bijection, so no result is lost or duplicated.}}{11}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:flatten}{{3}{11}{(a)~A binary tree with data at its leaves is a shape --- the tree with the data erased, with internal nodes~$\bullet $ and leaf positions~$\circ $ --- together with an assignment of data to the positions, as in \cite {AbbottAltenkirchGhaniMcBride04}. Positions occur wherever there is a leaf, at any depth. (b)~Flattening as an adapter from the tree interface to the list interface. The shape map sends the skeleton $s$ to its number of leaves, $\fn {Sum}\,s = 3$; the position map $\fn {flat}_s$ sends batch slot $i$ to the $i$-th leaf from the left, whatever its depth. It is a bijection, so no result is lost or duplicated}{figure.3}{}}
\newlabel{ex:conv-agent}{{3.10}{11}{A conversational agent and its window}{example.3.10}{}}
